/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Let v be the vehicle's forward speed in m/s, ω the wheel's angular speed in rad/s, and r the wheel radius in m.
   - v is vehicle forward speed (m/s); ω is wheel angular speed (rad/s); r is wheel radius (m); λ is slip ratio (dimensionless).
   - The tyre's friction coefficient μ depends on λ. μ is the ratio of friction force to normal load, so it has no unit.
   - For a drive wheel, wheel spin makes ωr larger than v.
   - Each wheel carries a toothed ring and a wheel speed sensor.
   - The hydraulic modulator sits between the master cylinder and each brake.
   - The ECU repeats build-hold-release about 5 to 15 times per second.
   - TCS uses the same wheel speed sensors.
   - Braking one spinning wheel also helps an open differential.
*/
