/* book exam traps: Understeer is corrected by braking the rear inner wheel; oversteer is corrected by braking the front outer wheel. Reversing them is the classic wrong answer. | Use radians in r = vδ/(L + K v²). Convert degrees to rad first; °/s is only for display. | ESP cannot raise tyre grip. It only uses the grip available; a car on ice still slides. | ESP is not ABS or TCS. ABS stops wheel lock; TCS stops drive-wheel spin; ESP corrects yaw. | Positive error rdes − rmeas means understeer, not oversteer. Keep the sign. */
