/* book exam traps: Skyhook damps the body, not the wheel; the wheel still follows the road. | Sign slip: F = −csky × vbody. Reversing the sign adds force in the direction of motion. | Semi-active can only dissipate energy; its force always opposes relative velocity across the damper and cannot hold the body flat over a bump. | Gain units: csky is N·s/m, not N/m (spring rate) or N·s (impulse). | The semi-active test uses vrel, not vbody. The same upward body velocity can be reachable or not, depending on whether the wheel moves down or up at that instant. */
